            <Keyword MajorTopicYN="N">• From a large representative sample of Swedish adolescents, we found that peritraumatic reactions in general, and specifically peritraumatic dissociation, seem to explain the relationship between a traumatic event and symptoms. • Peritraumatic dissociation was more frequent in males; intervention thoughts were more common for females. • Attention to peritraumatic reactions seems warranted in clinical settings as further research will expand the knowledge in this area.</Keyword>
